In this situation, the "dead end" corridor is likely not a dead end. 
Searching long enough at the end of this corridor would have probably 
found you a new path.

If not, pick the wall that is facing the largest unexplored area of the 
screen and search along it.  Remember that you do not have to search 
every square along this wall, as a search command will search wall 
spaces that are adjacent to you on the diagonals as well.

You should never come across a "bum" level.  There is always a way foreward.

Unless it is necessary in order to find the down staircase, I would not 
recommend searching at all in the early game.  It wastes time that could 
otherwise be spent securing a good food supply.  The same goes for 
pushing bolders, as the exertion makes you hungry faster.  If you feel 
it is necessary, come back up when you can be sure you won't starve to 
death.

